  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"rschema_0424\" contains four tables: User, System, Login_record, and System_authorization.\nThe User table represents a user of the system. It has columns for Account_status, Email, Last_login_time, Login_IP, Password, Phone_number, User_ID, and Username. These columns are all of type VARCHAR(255) and allow null values. The User_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe System table represents a system that the users can access. It has columns for Access_time, Approval_required, Callback_URL, Enabled, Secret_key, System_ID, System_domain, System_name, and Token_validity_period. These columns are all of type VARCHAR(255) or BOOL and allow null values. The System_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe Login_record table represents a login record of a user to a system. It has columns for Expiration_time, Login_IP, Login_time, Logout_time, System_ID, Token, User_ID, and Valid. The columns System_ID and User_ID are foreign keys referencing the System and User tables respectively. The combination of User_ID and System_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThe System_authorization table represents the authorization of a user to a system. It has columns for Authorization_time, Effective, Expiration_time, System_ID, and User_ID. The columns System_ID and User_ID are foreign keys referencing the System and User tables respectively. The combination of User_ID and System_ID is the primary key of this table.\nThis schema ensures referential integrity by enforcing foreign key constraints. When a record in the User or System table is deleted, the corresponding records in the Login_record and System_authorization tables will be automatically deleted to maintain the integrity of the data.",
  "gold_question": "This is a comprehensive system management platform. For user management, the system maintains basic user information including user ID, username, password, phone number, and email, while recording user status information including account status, last login time, and login IP. For system management, the platform maintains basic system information including system ID, system name, system domain, and access time, records system configuration information including callback URL, secret key, and token validity period, and manages system status including whether enabled and whether approval is required. For login records, the system maintains basic login information including user ID, system ID, login time, and login IP, records session information including token and expiration time, and manages login status including validity and logout time. For system authorization relationships, the platform maintains authorization information including user ID, system ID, and authorization time, and manages authorization status including whether effective and expiration time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0424.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0424\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_ip` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `account_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system` (\n  `system_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `system_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `system_domain` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `callback_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `secret_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `enabled` bool DEFAULT NULL,\n  `approval_required` bool DEFAULT NULL,\n  `access_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `token_validity_period` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`system_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `login_record` (\n  `user_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `system_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `login_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `logout_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `expiration_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `login_ip` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `valid` bool DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `system_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `login_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `login_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`system_id`) REFERENCES `system` (`system_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `system_authorization` (\n  `user_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `system_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `authorization_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `effective` bool DEFAULT NULL,\n  `expiration_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `system_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `system_authorization_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `system_authorization_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`system_id`) REFERENCES `system` (`system_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
